  "description": "Bean qou-cds2. Separates the two readings the bean holds at once: the convention-D Markov-Gram det = 3.998e-17 / cond 4.9e16 in float64 is consistent BOTH with an exactly singular form seen through f64 epsilon and with a merely ill-conditioned one, and the bean itself notes np.linalg.inv is 'inverting rounding noise'. Rebuilding the 6x6 Gram at 30/60/120 dps from pyhecke's own _nf_of_word_mp / NF_BASIS with z_D = q^3/(q^2+1) swapped for the hardcoded C spelling (gram.py has no D path; both gram_matrix_mp and z_mp hardcode 1/(sqrt q + sqrt(1/q)), a detector-blind C spelling) shows |det| collapsing with working precision under D while C stays non-singular -- i.e. the singularity is STRUCTURAL, an exact zero, not a conditioning artifact. This validates the aim of the named repair (quotient by the trace radical). Switches no convention, touches gram.py not at all, and proposes no value.",
